The plan:
Intake a big string, turn each word into an anagram mad libs style
Break down into list of words
Anagramize the words
Reconstruct the lists

Constraints:
Words from original string should be same anagram as other instances of same word
Anagrams already existing in the original string should not become the same anagram

For each word:
Check if already used
If so use the generated anagram
Otherwise generate a new anagram
Create a working list of anagrams (not including others that have been used or itself), and randomly assign them to the word
If no anagrams exist then return itself
With anagrams make one big beautiful string, include punctuation for flavor
For this maybe use a split into a string index inside of a for loop to find when and where the punctuation needs to be added?
Return new_story

Features:
Anagram a story
Set words to not anagramize (such as a setting for “for, to, if, when, the, a, etc…”, or also character names)
View transitions list button
whatever else we feel like throwing in there
